## About the project

This is a multi-page personal website for Satwik Raj, a Computer Science Engineering student. It was built as a Web Technology course project to practise the basics of front-end development: structuring content in HTML, styling it with an external stylesheet, and adding behaviour with JavaScript. There are no frameworks, libraries or build tools. Every page is a plain HTML file that opens directly in a browser.

## Objectives

- Build a small multi-page website with consistent navigation across pages
- Keep content, presentation and behaviour separate (HTML, CSS and JavaScript in their own files)
- Present a resume and personal details in a clear, readable format
- Host the finished site publicly with GitHub Pages

## Pages

| Page | File | Content |
|---|---|---|
| Home | `index.html` | Introduction, short About section, contact details, link to the resume |
| Resume | `resume.html` | Career objective, education, skills and a list of five projects |
| Bio-data | `biodata.html` | Personal details presented in a table |

Every page shares the same header and navigation bar (Home, About, Resume, Bio-data, Contact) and the same footer. The About and Contact links on the resume and bio-data pages point back to the matching sections on the home page.

## Web technology concepts used

- Semantic page structure with `header`, `nav`, `section` and `footer`
- Hyperlinks between pages and in-page anchors (`#about`, `#contact`)
- Data presented in HTML tables and lists
- One shared external stylesheet (`styles.css`) linked from every page
- One shared external script (`script.js`) loaded at the end of each page, used to fill in the current year in the footer
- A consistent layout reused across multiple pages

