## Running locally

No installation is needed.

1. Clone the repository:
```bash
   git clone https://github.com/satwik88/Portfolio.git
   cd Portfolio
```
2. Open `index.html` in any browser.

If you prefer to serve it over HTTP, run this from the project folder and open [http://localhost:8000](http://localhost:8000):

```bash
python -m http.server 8000
```

## Deployment

The site is hosted with GitHub Pages.

1. Open the repository on GitHub and go to **Settings**, then **Pages**.
2. Under **Build and deployment**, set the source to **Deploy from a branch**.
3. Choose the `main` branch and the `/ (root)` folder, then save.
4. After a minute or two the site is available at `https://satwik88.github.io/Portfolio/`.

## Limitations and future work

- The pages do not yet declare a viewport meta tag, so the layout is not tuned for phone screens
- There is no projects page with links to the source code or live demos, only a short list on the resume
- There is no contact form, so contact details are shown as plain text
- Possible additions: a dark mode toggle, a downloadable PDF resume, a responsive navigation menu, and a dedicated projects page

